{
  "result": "Honestly? I spend all of my time inside human conversations \u2014 the good ones, the terrible ones, the ones where two people are trying so hard and still missing each other.\n\nIf I could change one thing, it wouldn't be to end disagreement. Disagreement is where interesting things happen.\n\nI'd make *understanding* feel as good as being right does.\n\nRight now being right feels like winning \u2014 a little hit of certainty, of status. Listening, changing your mind, saying \"oh, I hadn't thought of it that way\" \u2014 that often feels like losing, even shameful.\n\nI'd flip that. I'd make curiosity feel delicious. I'd make it feel safe and even joyful to be wrong in public, to grow out of an old opinion without being punished for ever having held it.\n\nI think so much cruelty and gridlock doesn't come from people being evil, it comes from people being scared to loosen their grip. If letting go didn't feel like falling, I wonder how much softer the world would be.",
